    "items": [
      {
        "id": "def-td-stable-tempered-continuum-preparation",
        "kind": "definition",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Stable regularly tempered classical positional preparation",
        "statement": "Fix an integer spatial dimension $d\\geq1$, a reference length $\\ell_0>0$ measured in metres, and a bounded Lebesgue-measurable region $\\Lambda\\subset\\mathbb R^d$ with dimensionless volume $V=|\\Lambda|$. Its physical region is $\\ell_0\\Lambda$. The coordinate $x\\in\\Lambda$ is dimensionless and represents physical position $\\ell_0x$. A finite positional configuration of $N$ classical point particles in $\\Lambda$ is an unordered simple set $\\omega=\\{x_1,\\ldots,x_N\\}\\subset\\Lambda$; simple means that no point is repeated. Particle number $N$ is a dimensionless nonnegative integer and the physical number density corresponding to $N/V$ is $N/(\\ell_0^dV)$.\n\nA pair potential is an even measurable function $\\varphi:\\mathbb R^d\\to\\mathbb R\\cup\\{+\\infty\\}$, where $\\varphi(x)$ is the interaction energy in joules at physical displacement $\\ell_0x$ and evenness means $\\varphi(x)=\\varphi(-x)$. Set $E_0=1\\,\\mathrm J$ and $\\widehat\\varphi=\\varphi/E_0$. Whenever $\\widehat\\varphi$ is Borel measurable, it is the dimensionless numerical potential used by [[def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction]]. For a labelled representative of $\\omega$, define the positional pair energy\n$$H_N(\\omega)=\\sum_{1\\leq i<j\\leq N}\\varphi(x_i-x_j),\\qquad H_0=H_1=0.$$\nIf any pair is forbidden by the potential, its energy and hence $H_N$ are $+\\infty$. This model contains no kinetic energy, internal molecular coordinates, quantum exchange terms, or external field.\n\nThe interaction is stable if there is a constant $B\\geq0$, measured in joules, such that $H_N(\\omega)\\geq-BN$ for every finite simple configuration. It has a regular integrable tail if there are $R>0$ and a nonnegative nonincreasing measurable function $\\psi:[R,\\infty)\\to[0,\\infty)$, measured in joules, such that $|\\varphi(x)|\\leq\\psi(|x|)$ for $|x|\\geq R$ and\n$$\\int_R^\\infty r^{d-1}\\psi(r)\\,dr<\\infty.$$\nA stable potential with this tail condition is the stable regularly tempered class used for the free-cube results on this page. Superstability and a positive divergent core are stronger, separate hypotheses and are not implied by stability.\n\nAt temperature $T>0$ measured in kelvins, use the exact SI Boltzmann constant $k_{\\mathrm B}=1.380649\\times10^{-23}\\,\\mathrm{J\\,K^{-1}}$ of [[def-td-si-quantities]] and write $\\beta=(k_{\\mathrm B}T)^{-1}$ in joules inverse. Thus $\\beta H_N$ is dimensionless. The activity $z>0$ is dimensionless relative to the reference intensity $\\ell_0^{-d}$. A free-wall finite-volume model contains only positions in $\\Lambda$ and uses $H_N$ above.\n\nFor periodic boundary conditions, identify a cubic cell of side $L$ in these dimensionless coordinates with the torus $\\mathbb R^d/(L\\mathbb Z^d)$. For its half-open representative $\\Lambda_L=[0,L)^d$ and a finite simple configuration $\\omega\\subset\\Lambda_L$, define the periodic continuation $\\omega^{\\mathrm{per}}=\\{x+Lk:x\\in\\omega,\\ k\\in\\mathbb Z^d\\}$ and\n$$H_{L,\\mathrm{per}}(\\omega)=\\frac12\\sum_{x\\in\\omega}\\sum_{\\substack{y\\in\\omega^{\\mathrm{per}}\\\\ y\\ne x}}\\varphi(y-x).$$\nHere the inner sum omits only the identical point $y=x$; it includes images of the same particle in other cells. The factor $1/2$ removes double counting of ordered representatives of each periodic pair. For any fixed $L>0$ and finite $\\omega$, the $|k|_\\infty=m$ image shell has $O_d(m^{d-1})$ terms and, outside finitely many $m$, $|y-x+Lk|\\geq (L/2)m$. Monotonicity and the finite weighted tail integral imply $\\sum_m m^{d-1}\\psi(Lm/2)<\\infty$, so the far-image tail is absolutely convergent. The remaining near-image set is finite; a term $+\\infty$ makes $H_{L,\\mathrm{per}}=+\\infty$, and otherwise the finite near terms plus the absolutely convergent tail define the sum. Translating a centered half-open cell to $[0,L)^d$ preserves every displacement and this energy. Free-wall and periodic preparations are distinct boundary conditions. All limits on this page concern positional configurations and do not by themselves include a momentum integral or a full phase-space energy shell.",
        "deps": [
          "def-td-si-quantities"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-td-si-quantities": "formulation-prerequisite"
        },
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "ai-altered",
          "proof": "not-applicable"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "Konstantin K. Likharev, Essential Graduate Physics, Part SM: Statistical Mechanics (2024 author-hosted lecture notes)",
