        "physical_scope": "Only a named Borel-measurable stable regularly tempered model and parameter point on the positive-temperature branch or explicitly retained hard-core beta-zero branch for which the corresponding translation-invariant variational minimizer is assumed unique; no universal uniqueness or claim at coexistence.",
        "dependency_level": 6,
        "library": "physics"
      },
      {
        "id": "pthm-td-stable-tempered-free-cube-grand-pressure",
        "kind": "physics-theorem",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Stable-tempered free-cube grand pressure",
        "statement": "Assume AC. Let $d\\geq2$, $\\varphi$ be stable with the regular integrable tail of [[def-td-stable-tempered-continuum-preparation]], and assume its dimensionless representative $\\widehat\\varphi=\\varphi/E_0$ is Borel measurable, as required by the current mathematical supplier. Take $E_0=1\\,\\mathrm J$, $\\beta=(k_BT)^{-1}$, and $\\widehat\\beta=E_0\\beta>0$. For cubes $\\Lambda_L=[-L/2,L/2)^d$, let $\\Xi_L(z,\\beta)$ be the free-wall grand partition function specified by [[post-td-equilibrium-ensemble-sampling]]. Then the positional grand pressure\n$$p_L(z,T)=\\frac{k_BT}{\\ell_0^d|\\Lambda_L|}\\log\\Xi_L(z,\\beta)$$\nhas a finite limit as $L\\to\\infty$. In the dimensionless reference-volume convention of [[thm-tdmath-canonical-grand-duality]], let $P(\\alpha,\\widehat\\beta)=\\lim_{L\\to\\infty}|\\Lambda_L|^{-1}\\log\\Xi_L(e^\\alpha,\\widehat\\beta)$, where the supplier uses numerical energies in units of $E_0$. Then $p=(k_BT/\\ell_0^d)P(\\log z,\\widehat\\beta)$. This is a conditional model deduction, not a measurement or an assertion that every real gas realizes the preparation.",
        "deps": [
          "def-axiom-of-choice",
          "def-td-stable-tempered-continuum-preparation",
          "post-td-equilibrium-ensemble-sampling",
          "thm-tdmath-canonical-grand-duality"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-axiom-of-choice": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-td-stable-tempered-continuum-preparation": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "post-td-equilibrium-ensemble-sampling": "physical-assumption",
          "thm-tdmath-canonical-grand-duality": "mathematical-premise"
        },
        "provenance": {
