      {
        "id": "pthm-td-controlled-continuum-thermodynamic-limit",
        "kind": "physics-theorem",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Controlled continuum interval-energy thermodynamic limit",
        "statement": "Assume AC, the ultrafilter extension principle, DC, and HB, as required by the current variational-pressure supplier. Let $E_0=1\\,\\mathrm J$, $\\widehat\\varphi=\\varphi/E_0$, and assume $\\widehat\\varphi$ is Borel measurable. Require the exact superstable regular hypotheses of [[def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction]] for this dimensionless potential: a stable part plus a nonnegative core part bounded below by a positive constant on an $\\ell^\\infty$-ball, with the supplier's lower and upper regular tail conditions. Use $\\widehat H=H/E_0$, $\\widehat\\beta=E_0\\beta$ for $\\beta>0$, and $\\widehat e=e/E_0$; then $\\beta H=\\widehat\\beta\\widehat H$. For this supplier convention, let $\\nu$ be the supremum of finite-entropy, finite-energy attainable densities for $\\widehat\\varphi$, and write $\\widehat\\Phi(P)$ for the supplier's limiting positional energy density; let $e_0(\\rho)=\\inf\\{\\widehat\\Phi(P):\\rho(P)=\\rho,\\ I(P)<\\infty\\}$ be its numerical positional-energy infimum. Let $D\\subset[0,\\infty)$ be a nondegenerate density interval, and require $\\inf D<\\nu$ and $\\widehat e>\\inf_{\\rho\\in D}e_0(\\rho)$. Use the supplier's periodic cubes $\\Lambda_n$ of numerical volume $V_n=|\\Lambda_n|$ and define explicitly\n$$A_n=\\{\\omega:N_{\\Lambda_n}(\\omega)/V_n\\in D,\\ H_{n,\\mathrm{per}}(\\omega)/(E_0V_n)\\le\\widehat e\\},\\qquad \\widehat e=e/E_0.$$\nHere $H_{n,\\mathrm{per}}$ is the physical positional energy in joules in the same periodic convention; equivalently its event inequality is $H_{n,\\mathrm{per}}/V_n\\le e$. For every $n$ with positive event probability, the prepared law is $R_n(B)=Q_{\\Lambda_n}(B\\cap A_n)/Q_{\\Lambda_n}(A_n)$ on the finite count sigma-algebra. Equivalently, with $M_n=\\sum_{N\\ge0}\\mu_{\\Lambda_n,N}$, $R_n(B)=M_n(B\\cap A_n)/M_n(A_n)$, since $Q_{\\Lambda_n}=e^{-V_n}M_n$; use the count-sigma restriction of these positional measures. This defines the density-interval/upper-energy conditional preparation and its conditioned laws. For $\\beta>0$, the finite-volume grand and microcanonical weights are those of [[post-td-equilibrium-ensemble-sampling]]. For $\\beta=0$, require a nonempty hard-core displacement set and use the formal retained-admissibility continuation of [[def-td-retained-hard-core-zero-beta-preparation]]; do not interpret $0\\cdot(+\\infty)$.\n\nFor both the positive-$\\beta$ branch and the formal retained-hard-core $\\beta=0$ branch, [[thm-tdmath-interval-event-ensemble-limit]] gives eventual event positivity, the constrained entropy-rate limit, and common-minimizer accumulation points; at $\\beta=0$, [[thm-tdmath-retained-hard-zero-beta-limit]] identifies the matching retained grand law and minimizer set. If the relevant common minimizer set is the singleton adopted in [[post-td-grand-variational-phase-uniqueness]] for the multiplier pair supplied by that branch, both the conditioned laws and the corresponding periodic grand laws converge locally to $P^\\ast$ for every measurable local observable $f$ with $|f|\\leq c(1+N_A)$ on a bounded region $A$. This is an interval-density and upper-energy result, not a fixed-particle-number or shrinking-shell theorem.\n\n\nHere local observables are evaluated on the periodic continuation of the prepared torus configuration. This is the same periodic boundary preparation, with no new physical sampling assumption; a configuration is not extended by the empty configuration outside its fundamental cube.",
        "deps": [
          "def-axiom-of-choice",
          "def-ultrafilter-extension-principle",
          "def-dependent-choice",
          "def-hahn-banach-extension-principle-relative",
          "def-td-stable-tempered-continuum-preparation",
          "def-td-retained-hard-core-zero-beta-preparation",
