      {
        "id": "pthm-td-controlled-thermodynamic-ensemble-duality",
        "kind": "physics-theorem",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Controlled canonical–grand thermodynamic duality",
        "statement": "Assume AC and $T>0$, with $\\beta=(k_BT)^{-1}$. Under the stable regularly tempered positional model of [[def-td-stable-tempered-continuum-preparation]] and the adopted ensemble weights of [[post-td-equilibrium-ensemble-sampling]], assume the dimensionless potential $\\widehat\\varphi=\\varphi/E_0$ is Borel measurable as required by the current mathematical carriers. Set $E_0=1\\,\\mathrm J$ and $\\widehat\\beta=E_0\\beta$; write $F(\\rho,\\beta)$ and $P(\\alpha,\\beta)$ for the mathematical rates evaluated at $\\widehat\\beta$. Let $F(\\rho,\\beta)$ be the canonical log-partition rate per dimensionless reference volume, defined on interior attainable densities by the fixed-density limit and extended to the closed effective density domain by the upper-semicontinuous concave extension specified in [[thm-tdmath-canonical-grand-duality]]. Let\n$$P(\\alpha,\\beta)=\\lim_{V\\to\\infty}V^{-1}\\log\\sum_{N\\geq0}e^{\\alpha N}Z(V,N),\\qquad \\alpha=\\log z.$$\nThen\n$$P(\\alpha,\\beta)=\\sup_{\\rho\\geq0}\\{F(\\rho,\\beta)+\\alpha\\rho\\},\\qquad F(\\rho,\\beta)=\\inf_{\\alpha\\in\\mathbb R}\\{P(\\alpha,\\beta)-\\alpha\\rho\\}.$$\nIn physical units, $p=(k_BT/\\ell_0^d)P$ and the positional Helmholtz free-energy density is $f_{\\mathrm{pos}}=-(k_BT/\\ell_0^d)F$, with the fixed reference normalization of [[post-td-classical-indistinguishable-particle-measure]]. This duality concerns limiting thermodynamic functions only. It does not imply local ensemble equivalence, uniqueness of a phase, or convergence at excluded density endpoints.",
        "deps": [
          "def-axiom-of-choice",
          "def-td-stable-tempered-continuum-preparation",
          "post-td-equilibrium-ensemble-sampling",
          "post-td-classical-indistinguishable-particle-measure",
          "thm-tdmath-canonical-interior-density-limit",
          "thm-tdmath-canonical-grand-duality"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
