      {
        "id": "pthm-td-interacting-three-ensemble-local-limit",
        "kind": "physics-theorem",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Interacting exact-N shrinking-shell three-ensemble local limit",
        "statement": "Assume AC, the ultrafilter extension principle, DC, and HB as required by the current variational-pressure supplier. Let $E_0=1\\,\\mathrm J$, $\\widehat\\varphi=\\varphi/E_0$, and assume $\\widehat\\varphi$ is Borel measurable. Require the exact superstable regular hypotheses of [[def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction]]; use $\\widehat H=H/E_0$ and $\\widehat\\beta=E_0\\beta>0$ in its mathematical suppliers. Let $F(\\rho,\\beta)$ denote the numerical canonical rate evaluated at $\\widehat\\beta$; assume it is differentiable in physical $\\beta$ at the chosen temperature and set $e=-\\partial_\\beta F(\\rho,\\beta)$, in joules per dimensionless reference volume. For periodic cubes $\\Lambda_n$, take exact particle numbers $N_n$ with $N_n/V_n\\to\\rho$ at a positive interior attainable density. Choose a finite supporting activity parameter $\\alpha$ for $F$ at $\\rho$ and set $z=e^\\alpha>0$; assume the corresponding stationary grand variational minimizer is the singleton $P^\\ast$ as in [[post-td-grand-variational-phase-uniqueness]].\n\nThen there exists a constructed sequence $\\delta_n\\downarrow0$ for which the periodic exact-$N_n$ canonical positional law, the periodic grand-canonical law at $(\\alpha,\\beta)$, and the uniform positional shell law of [[def-td-controlled-fixed-n-energy-shell]] on\n$$N=N_n,\\qquad |H_{L_n,\\mathrm{per}}/V_n-e|\\leq\\delta_n,\\qquad L_n=2n+1$$\nall converge locally to $P^\\ast$. Convergence means convergence of expectations for every measurable local observable $f$ supported in a bounded region and satisfying $|f|\\leq c(1+N_A)$ there. The shell sequence is constructed from canonical concentration; arbitrary preassigned shrinking widths, exact zero-width surfaces, full phase-space shells involving kinetic momentum, and a conclusion at nonunique minimizers are not asserted.\n\nHere local observables are evaluated on the periodic continuation of the prepared torus configuration. This is the same periodic boundary preparation, with no new physical sampling assumption; a configuration is not extended by the empty configuration outside its fundamental cube.",
        "deps": [
          "def-axiom-of-choice",
