      {
        "id": "pthm-td-qualified-van-hove-and-exterior-limit",
        "kind": "physics-theorem",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Qualified van Hove and tempered-exterior thermodynamic limits",
        "statement": "Assume AC, as required by the current mathematical definition and its shape suppliers. Let $d\\geq2$, $E_0=1\\,\\mathrm J$, $\\widehat\\varphi=\\varphi/E_0$, and assume $\\widehat\\varphi$ is Borel measurable and superstable and regular as in [[def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction]]. Use $\\widehat H=H/E_0$ and $\\widehat\\beta=E_0(k_BT)^{-1}>0$ in the mathematical rates. Let $(\\Lambda_k)$ be a van Hove sequence as in [[def-td-admissible-van-hove-and-tempered-exterior]]. First, for free walls, the positional grand pressure along $\\Lambda_k$ converges to the free-cube pressure of [[pthm-td-stable-tempered-free-cube-grand-pressure]]. For any positive interior attainable density $\\rho$ and exact integers $N_k$ with $N_k/|\\Lambda_k|\\to\\rho$, the exact-$N_k$ free-wall canonical log-partition rate converges to the same cube canonical rate. These two shape statements require superstability and regularity; stability alone is not asserted to suffice for arbitrary van Hove shapes.\n\nSecond, strengthen the potential hypothesis: for some $r_0>0$, $\\widehat\\varphi(x)\\geq\\widehat\\chi(\\|x\\|_\\infty)>0$ whenever $0<\\|x\\|_\\infty\\leq r_0$, where $\\widehat\\chi$ is nonincreasing and $\\int_0^{r_0}\\widehat\\chi(r)r^{d-1}\\,dr=+\\infty$. For each fixed $t<\\infty$, the free-wall grand pressure in $\\Lambda_n$ with exterior $\\zeta\\in\\Omega(t)$ then converges uniformly in $\\zeta$ to the same free-cube pressure. The exterior interaction is the deterministic positional term of [[def-td-admissible-van-hove-and-tempered-exterior]], not a volume-filling external field. This genuine divergent-core condition is the exact stronger hypothesis of the current exterior supplier; it is not inferred from superstability or replaced by a weaker source condition.",
        "deps": [
          "def-axiom-of-choice",
          "def-td-stable-tempered-continuum-preparation",
          "def-td-admissible-van-hove-and-tempered-exterior",
          "post-td-equilibrium-ensemble-sampling",
          "pthm-td-stable-tempered-free-cube-grand-pressure",
          "def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction",
          "thm-tdmath-superstable-van-hove-pressure",
          "thm-tdmath-van-hove-fixed-n-limit",
          "thm-tdmath-uniform-tempered-exterior-pressure"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-axiom-of-choice": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-td-stable-tempered-continuum-preparation": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "def-td-admissible-van-hove-and-tempered-exterior": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "post-td-equilibrium-ensemble-sampling": "physical-assumption",
          "pthm-td-stable-tempered-free-cube-grand-pressure": "physical-result",
          "def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-tdmath-superstable-van-hove-pressure": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-tdmath-van-hove-fixed-n-limit": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-tdmath-uniform-tempered-exterior-pressure": "mathematical-premise"
        },
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "ai-altered",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "Hans-Otto Georgii, Large deviations and the equivalence of ensembles for Gibbsian particle systems with superstable interaction, Probability Theory and Related Fields 99 (1994), 171–195",
              "url": "https://www.mathematik.uni-muenchen.de/~georgii/papers/LDPsuperstable.pdf"
            },
            {
              "title": "David Ruelle, Superstable Interactions in Classical Statistical Mechanics, Communications in Mathematical Physics 18 (1970), 127–159",
              "url": "https://www.ihes.fr/~ruelle/PUBLICATIONS/%5B28%5D.pdf"
            },
            {
              "title": "David Tong, Statistical Physics (author-hosted Cambridge lecture notes)",
              "url": "https://davidtong.org/teaching/statistical-physics/statmechhtml/S1"
            },
            {
              "title": "Konstantin K. Likharev, Essential Graduate Physics, Part SM: Statistical Mechanics (2024 author-hosted lecture notes)",
              "url": "https://phys.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Thermodynamics_and_Statistical_Mechanics/Essential_Graduate_Physics_-_Statistical_Mechanics_%28Likharev%29/03%3A_Ideal_and_Not-So-Ideal_Gases/3.05%3A_Gases_of_weakly_interacting_particles"
            }
          ]
        },
        "physical_scope": "Classical positional Borel pair systems in dimension at least two; van Hove free-wall limits require superstability and regularity, while deterministic exterior limits additionally require a genuine positive divergent core in the supplier's infinity norm and a fixed uniformly tempered exterior class.",
        "dependency_level": 7,
        "library": "physics",
        "proof_strategy": "direct"
      }
    ]
