        "id": "ex-td-two-particle-hard-core-preparation",
        "kind": "example",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Two indistinguishable hard-core particles in an interval",
        "statement": "Take a dimensionless interval $\\Lambda=[0,L]$ with $0<a<L$, two identical particles, and the hard-core pair potential $\\varphi(r)=+\\infty$ for $|r|<a$ and $0$ otherwise. At any positive temperature the configurational canonical partition function is independent of $T$ and equals\n$$Z_{\\Lambda,2}=\\frac12(L-a)^2.$$\nThe factor $1/2$ is the adopted indistinguishable positional measure. This finite-volume calculation has no momentum variables or experimental data.",
        "deps": [
          "def-td-stable-tempered-continuum-preparation",
          "post-td-classical-indistinguishable-particle-measure",
          "post-td-equilibrium-ensemble-sampling"
        ],
