        "proof_strategy": "direct"
      },
      {
        "id": "ex-td-volume-sized-external-field",
        "kind": "example",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "A volume-filling field changes ideal-gas pressure",
        "statement": "For the ideal positional gas $\\varphi=0$ in a region of dimensionless volume $V$, the grand partition is $\\Xi_V(z,\\beta)=e^{zV}$. Now impose an external energy $c$ joules per particle at every point of the volume. The new grand partition is $\\Xi_V^{(c)}=e^{ze^{-\\beta c}V}$, so the dimensionless pressure rate changes from $z$ to $ze^{-\\beta c}$ when $c\\neq0$. This exact volume-filling external preparation is not a member of the deterministic exterior class used by [[pthm-td-qualified-van-hove-and-exterior-limit]].",
        "deps": [
